meta {
  name: AutoReserveringCancelClampAnnuleer
  type: http
  seq: 65
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/bon/{{autoresCancelBonnr}}/annuleer
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.stempel: eq O
}

docs {
  Cancels the bon created by AutoReserveringCancelClampSetup, which has
  an under-reserved bonlijn (gereserv 2 < teLeveren 100, from
  AutoReserveringCancelClampCreateLijn). Before the clamp fix in
  Luna.BusinessLogic.BonBE (ReleaseReservationsForBon/
  ReleaseBomReservations), this cancel would have subtracted the FULL
  te-leveren (100) from artikel.besteld-kl even though only 2 was ever
  added, pushing besteld-kl to -98. The 200 response here only proves
  the cancel doesn't error - the actual clamp effect (besteld-kl staying
  at/above 0) is NOT observable through any exposed GET endpoint (no API
  exposes besteld-kl/pbesteld-kl) and was confirmed via direct ABL/DB
  query during backend-coder implementation - see the handoff note for
  the exact before/after values (besteld-kl 0 -> 0 clamped, and for the
  BOM-component clamp case, a component's pbesteld-kl 8 -> 0 clamped
  instead of going to -2). Requires {{autoresCancelBonnr}}.
}
